Description: Run rustbook from the book source directory
 Rust 1.93's reference book invokes the in-tree mdbook-spec plugin via a
 relative manifest path in book.toml. When bootstrap runs rustbook from the
 source root, mdbook resolves that path against the wrong directory and the
 documentation build aborts on Launchpad. Execute rustbook from the book's
 source directory so mdbook resolves local plugin paths correctly.
Author: Codex <codex@example.org>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-07-07

--- a/src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/doc.rs
+++ b/src/bootstrap/src/core/build_steps/doc.rs
@@ -166,6 +166,7 @@
                 builder.add_rustc_lib_path(compiler, &mut rustbook_cmd);
             }
 
+            rustbook_cmd.current_dir(&src);
             rustbook_cmd
                 .arg("build")
                 .arg(&src)
@@ -183,6 +184,7 @@
 
                 builder
                     .tool_cmd(Tool::Rustbook)
+                    .current_dir(&src)
                     .arg("build")
                     .arg(&src)
                     .arg("-d")
                     .arg("-d")
